
  <sn><md>### String Literals in C

A **string literal** is a sequence of characters written directly in a C program and enclosed in **double quotation marks (`" "`)**.

Examples:

```c
"Hello"
"Emon"
"Hello World"
"12345"
```

Here, `"Hello"` is a **string literal**.

</md></sn>
